<title>USA: L.L. BEAN SAYS PACKAGE DELIVERY UNINTERRUPTED.</title>
<headline>L.L. BEAN SAYS PACKAGE DELIVERY UNINTERRUPTED.</headline>
<dateline>FREEPORT, Maine 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>L.L. Bean said Friday that despite a strike by 185,000 union workers at United Parcel Service it's package deliveries continue uninterrupted.</p>
<p>The outdoor outfitter said that because of a preferred relationship with Federal Express, a competing package delivery service, product delivery has not experienced any disruptions.</p>
<p>L.L. Bean said it's customer service representatives have been handling an increase in calls from customers, anxious that the delivery of their orders might somehow be affected.</p>
</text>
